  "service": "Vertex AI",
  "title": "Vertex AI: New Serving Profiles, Breaking Changes & Scope Updates",
  "summary": "Vertex AI introduces a new `ServingProfile` resource for managing model serving configurations. This update also includes several breaking changes, notably making `parent` and `name` parameters strictly required, and changing the type of `structuredPrompt` in vision models. OAuth scopes for `agents` methods have also been adjusted.",
  "details": "Developers can now manage `ServingProfile` resources with new `create`, `get`, `list`, `patch`, and `delete` methods under `projects.locations.servingProfiles`, providing dedicated control over model serving configurations. \n\nThis update includes several breaking changes: The `parent` and `name` parameters are now strictly required for new `ServingProfile` methods and potentially others, continuing a trend from previous updates. Additionally, several properties are now read-only: `nextPageToken` and `servingProfiles` in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ListServingProfilesResponse`, `createTime` and `updateTime` in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ServingProfile`, and `gcsMetricsUri` in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1TuningJob`. Crucially, the `structuredPrompt` property in `CloudAiLargeModelsVisionExperimentsResponseProEditResult` and `CloudAiLargeModelsVisionGenerateVideoExperimentsProEditConfig` has changed its type from `object` to `string`, requiring immediate code updates if you were using these fields.\n\nFor `projects.locations.agents` methods (create, delete, get, list, patch), the primary OAuth scope has shifted to `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/aiplatform`, promoting the Principle of Least Privilege, though `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/cloud-platform` remains supported. Finally, the `projects.updateCacheConfig` method now supports an `updateMask` parameter for more precise updates to cache settings, including `disable_cache` and `retention_config`.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 9,
  "tags": [
    "AI/ML",
    "Vertex AI",
    "Breaking Change",
    "New Feature",
    "Security"
  ],
